👉 String Memory in Java -> Java stores String objects in a special memory area called the String Pool to improve memory efficiency.
                             The String Pool is a special area in the Heap Memory where Java stores unique string literals.

              Heap Memory
+---------------------------------------+
|                                       |
|      String Pool (Special Area)       |
|                                       |
|      "Java"                           |
|      "Python"                         |
|      "Hello"                          |
|                                       |
+---------------------------------------+

👉 == Operator -> The == operator compares object references (memory addresses), not the contents.

    String s1 = "Java";
    String s2 = "Java";
    System.out.println(s1 == s2);   // True

👉 equals() -> The equals() method compares the contents of two strings.

    String s1 = new String("Java");
    String s2 = new String("Java");
    System.out.println(s1.equals(s2));

👉 intern() Method -> The intern() method returns a reference from the String Pool.

    String s1 = new String("Java");
    String s2 = s1.intern();
    String s3 = "Java";
    System.out.println(s2 == s3);


